cts 5:36). He headed an insurrection against the Roman authority. Beyond this nothing is known of him.","status":"publish","name_meaning":{"meaning":"flowing with water","hebrew":"תּוֹדָס","translit":"tudas","strongs":"none","greek":"Θευδᾶς","greekTranslit":"Theuda͂s"}},"thomas_2851":{"id":"thomas_2851","name":"Thomas","title":"Thomas","gender":"Male","min":31,"max":33,"aka":["Didymus"],"father":[],"mother":[],"partners":[],"children":[],"siblings":[],"birthPlace":[],"deathPlace":[],"events":[],"verses":[23420,24306,25161,26539,26673,26891,26893,26894,26895,26896,26900,26936],"verseCount":12,"dict":"twin, one of the twelve (Matthew 10:3 ; Mark 3:18 , etc.). He was also called Didymus (John 11:16 ; 20:24), which is the Greek equivalent of the Hebrew name. All we know regarding him is recorded in the fourth Gospel (John 11:15 John 11:16 ; John 14:4 John 14:5 ; John 20:24 John 20:25 John 20:26-29). From the circumstance that in the lists of the apostles he is always mentioned along with Matthew, who was the son of Alphaeus (Mark 3:18), and that these two are always followed by James, who was also the son of Alphaeus, it has been supposed that these three, Matthew, Thomas, and James, were brothers.","status":"publish","name_meaning":{"meaning":"a twin","hebrew":"תֹּאמָא","translit":"toma","strongs":"none","greek":"Θωμᾶς","greekTranslit":"Thōma͂s"}},"tiberius_2852":{"id":"tiberius_2852","name":"Tiberius","title":"Tiberius","gender":"Male","min":26,"max":26,"aka":[],"father":[],"mother":[],"partners":[],"children":[],"siblings":[],"birthPlace":[],"deathPlace":[],"events":[],"verses":[25026],"verseCount":1,"status":"wip","name_meaning":{"meaning":"the son of Tiber"}},"tibni_2853":{"id":"tibni_2853","name":"Tibni","title":"Tibni","gender":"Male","min":-929,"max":-929,"aka":[],"father":["ginath_1320"],"mother":[],"partners":[],"children":[],"siblings":[],"birthPlace":[],"deathPlace":[],"events":[],"verses":[9304,9305],"verseCount":2,"status":"wip","name_meaning":{"meaning"