us","gender":"Male","min":58,"max":58,"aka":[],"father":[],"mother":[],"partners":[],"children":[],"siblings":[],"birthPlace":[],"deathPlace":[],"events":[],"verses":[27594],"verseCount":1,"dict":"prince, a Greek rhetorician, in whose \"school\" at Ephesus Paul disputed daily for the space of two years with those who came to him (Acts 19:9). Some have supposed that he was a Jew, and that his \"school\" was a private synagogue.","status":"publish","name_meaning":{"meaning":"a prince; one that reigns","hebrew":"טִירָנוֹס","translit":"tiyranos","strongs":"none","greek":"Τύραννος","greekTranslit":"Túrannos"}}}